  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Inside the client",
      "items": [
        "Resource façades: Warehouses, Projects, Roles, Users, Server, Permissions; one call per operation, errors as *client.APIError",
        "The auth round-tripper sets the Authorization header on every request; retryablehttp retries 429 and 5xx above it",
        "The generated APIClient is embedded as the escape hatch for operations without a façade"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Layer rule",
      "items": [
        "lkctl reaches the Management API only through the resource façades",
        "A forbidigo rule in .golangci.yml rejects cmd/ references to the generated services",
        "An operation without a façade gets a façade method first"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authentication",
      "items": [
        "Three auth sources: OAuth2 client credentials, static access token, Kubernetes service account token",
        "Only client credentials fetches a token from the identity provider; Lakekeeper validates tokens against it",
        "CatalogV1 passes the same auth source's token to iceberg-go"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Server side",
      "items": [
        "The SDK is a client: it runs none of the server-side components",
        "make test-integration brings them up with docker-compose: Lakekeeper, PostgreSQL, OpenFGA, MinIO and Keycloak",
        "Secret storage is optional: by default Lakekeeper keeps secrets encrypted in PostgreSQL"
      ]
    }
  ]
